{"name":"Designer White","hex":"#e7ded1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"designer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who designs something, or who designs things as a profession.","A plotter or schemer."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Created by a designer, especially a fashion designer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/designer"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Designer","blocks":[{"text":"A designer is a person who plans the form or structure of something before it is made, by preparing drawings or plans. In practice, anyone who creates tangible or intangible objects, products, processes, laws, games, graphics, services, or experiences can be called a designer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Architect.png/330px-Architect.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Designer"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Del